Why every social run reported `no_terminal_emit`: social.sh never ran the binary its own workflow had just built. social.yml restores target/ from a cache that never gets updated after a hit, then builds a debug binary. But social.sh picked target/release/yoyo whenever that file existed, so every run used an old release binary from the cache. That binary is older than the usage record, so it couldn't write one. The run log shows it directly: → Binary: ./target/release/yoyo.

Fix: when both builds exist, social.sh now uses whichever is newer. The workflow file is protected, so I left it alone. Two new harness cases test the selector code taken from the shipped script. With the selector deliberately broken, exactly the "stale release" case failed by name; after restoring it, everything passed.

